    "rawResponseText": "An owner in Mexico looking for **affiliation without a fully standardized hard brand** should primarily evaluate **soft brands / collection brands** from **Wyndham, Hilton, Choice, Marriott, Hyatt, IHG, Best Western, and possibly Accor**. These brands are designed to preserve more of a hotel’s independent identity while still giving access to distribution, loyalty, and marketing support.[8][13][15][16]\n\nThe most relevant options shown in the results for **Mexico** are:\n\n- **Wyndham: Trademark Collection by Wyndham** — explicitly described as a soft brand, and it has already debuted in Mexico with Acanto Hotel Playa del Carmen.[1]\n- **Wyndham: Registry Collection Hotels** — also a soft brand, positioned for upper-upscale/luxury independent or distinctive properties; Wyndham notes a Mexico property in this collection.[11][6]\n- **Hilton: Curio Collection by Hilton** — a soft brand for independent hotels, with Hilton identifying it as one of its flexible soft-brand options in Mexico.[3][7]\n- **Hilton: Tapestry Collection by Hilton** — another Hilton soft brand; Hilton cites it as part of its Mexico soft-brand strategy.[3]\n- **Hilton: LXR Hotels & Resorts** — Hilton’s luxury soft-brand option, also cited as a soft brand in the Mexico context.[3]\n- **Choice Hotels: Ascend Hotel Collection** — described by Choice as an upscale soft brand for independent hotels, and it already has properties in Mexico.[2][4]\n- **Marriott: Autograph Collection / Luxury Collection / Tribute Portfolio** — these are established Marriott soft/collection brands commonly used for independent hotels, though the search results here do not specifically show a Mexico launch for each.[16]\n- **Hyatt: Unbound Collection** — a collection brand for independent hotels, suitable if the owner wants a softer affiliation model.[16]\n- **Best Western: BW Signature Collection / BW Premier Collection / SureStay Collection** — collection-style options for owners seeking brand support with more individuality.[14][16]\n- **IHG: Voco** and **Six Senses**-adjacent soft-brand approaches — IHG is cited as offering flexible choices, including soft-brand-like positioning, though the clearest Mexico-specific evidence in the results is limited.[9]\n\nIf the goal is specifically **Mexico affiliation with minimal standardization**, the strongest evidence-backed shortlist from the results is:\n\n- **Trademark Collection by Wyndham**\n- **Registry Collection Hotels**\n- **Curio Collection by Hilton**\n- **Tapestry Collection by Hilton**\n- **LXR Hotels & Resorts**\n- **Ascend Hotel Collection**\n\nFor an owner choosing among them, the practical split is:\n\n- **Upper-midscale to upscale conversions:** Trademark Collection, Ascend Hotel Collection[1][2][4]\n- **Upscale to luxury independent hotels:** Curio, Tapestry, LXR, Registry Collection, Autograph/Luxury Collection/Tribute Portfolio[3][11][16]\n\nIf you want, I can turn this into a **Mexico-focused shortlist by hotel type** — for example, *boutique city hotel, resort, all-inclusive, or luxury conversion*.",
